                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2782fcb1-688c-3925-b75f-7f100c92134d",
                        "entry_id": "dbfee8eb-3d72-3539-8f8c-9015422801a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "действие по значению гл. смягчать, смягчить, смягчаться, смягчиться"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdecbb11-db54-43f5-a0fa-48eed24d1361",
                                "sense_id": "2782fcb1-688c-3925-b75f-7f100c92134d",
                                "text": "Но я верю, вы сами, дорогие читатели, вот-вот прочтёте, что и как хотите, с купюрами, без купюр, со смягчениями или усилениями, кому как будет угодно, я же не беру греха на душу в эту минуту: ни сокращать, ни редактировать, оскоплять Алешковского не могу."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef787790-2f48-3b2c-b726-1de13f2cc46b",
                        "entry_id": "dbfee8eb-3d72-3539-8f8c-9015422801a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "лингв. произнесение с дополнительным к основной артикуляции подъёмом средней части спинки языка к твёрдому нёбу; палатализация"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e776a31a-2ce7-4d56-ba64-920a7e044d5e",
                        "source_entry_id": "dbfee8eb-3d72-3539-8f8c-9015422801a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "mitigation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mitigation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                        "entry_id": "64993727-357e-37a5-bcd2-81b98a4092c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A reduction or decrease of something harmful or unpleasant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c10c3f6f-b55f-4c30-96fd-6b8df97f0a37",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Two golden hours, in which the astonishing news of the intended party was revealed to Louisa, with all of its contrivances, expenses, and mitigations, so far as they were elucidated, were given and said to be \"done in her honour;\"..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f671c655-56bd-45c9-a73d-fda9a1487f03",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "One possible drought mitigation strategy for Afghanistan is to divert excess water from water-rich river basins to water-scarce river basins in cases where this is technologically, economically and environmentally feasible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02e96060-23e6-49aa-982e-f780a99f6f30",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Much of the arable land acquired by HS2 is being used for mitigation planting, in an attempt to achieve the goal set by HS2 Ltd for Phase 1, which will mean there should be no measurable loss of biodiversity after construction of the line compared with what was there before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d747c713-8591-45d2-8015-b6a36ccb0932",
                                                "sense_id": "493875a2-2de4-3ff9-95dd-0d1d0f2b6abb",
                                                "text": "Its [the gantry crane's] noise-mitigation characteristics even include a soft-landing feature to minimise the noise when containers are lowered."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0f1e3ccc-cd2d-4cd7-86c5-17607452dd99",
                        "source_entry_id": "dbfee8eb-3d72-3539-8f8c-9015422801a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "alleviation",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alleviation",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9c351a8-939e-3bda-bddc-638be1524fc0",
                                        "entry_id": "65e69325-0fde-3165-b62e-9abf6f3eeac6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of alleviating; relief or mitigation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4834678f-114b-4d75-818e-56bb46c7643c",
                                                "sense_id": "d9c351a8-939e-3bda-bddc-638be1524fc0",
                                                "text": "The only light is from a high barred window, and it is not so much light as an alleviation of the murk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b180f8f9-6460-3277-be44-00da9189a7b7",
                                        "entry_id": "65e69325-0fde-3165-b62e-9abf6f3eeac6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "the act of reducing pain or anything else unpleasant; easement"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
